    <statement><p>(A) Find the parametric equations for the line through the point 
P = (5, -1, 0) that is perpendicular to the plane
<m>3 x  - 1 y  - 5 z = 1.</m></p>
<p>Use "t" as your variable, t = 0 should correspond to P, and the velocity 
vector of the line should be the same as the standard normal vector of the plane.</p>
<p>x = <fillin characters="8" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p>y = <fillin characters="8" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
<p>z = <fillin characters="8" name="AnSwEr0003"/></p>
<p>(B) At what point Q does this line intersect the yz-plane?</p>
<p>Q = (<fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0004"/>, <fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0005"/>, <fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0006"/>)</p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>5+t\cdot 3</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>-1+t\mathopen{}\left(-1\right)</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>0+t\mathopen{}\left(-5\right)</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>0</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>0.666666666666667</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
